'''Enmu''' (魘夢, ''Enmu'') is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy that appears in the [[Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 15.1 Update#Version 15.1.1 Update|Version 15.1.1]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Enmu
|image = E 762.png
|first appearance = [[Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Collaboration Event#Mugen Train|Mugen Train]]
|money drop = 2,500¢ - 9,875¢
}}

==Enemy==
Enmu is the second most difficult enemy to deal with in the Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Collaboration Event. He boasts a huge [[Omni Strike]] that hits up to 700 range from where they stand at 400, as well as a 4-second [[Freeze]] that makes him a decent CC against the units he doesn't instantly kill. This completely invalidates the use of most traditional ranged attackers, meaning you'll have to fight him head-on. The strongest you'll see him is in [[Go To Sleeeeep...]] {{2c}} and [[Lower Rank One - Enmu (Merciless)]], where he has nearly 1,000,000 HP and 40,000 AP in both stages.

==Strategy==
Due to Enmu's huge Omni Strike, the best way to counter him is with fast attackers like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]], and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]. He can be crowd-controlled by [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|Anti-Traitless Cats]] such as [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Glass Cat]] or [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]], or outranged by using [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]]/Ubers that have over 700 range.

[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] in particular makes quick work of Enmu with they're piercing Wave Attacks, and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] be used to rush him down for timed-rewards in later stages.

